{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1436092,
  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197580",
      "title": "Setting Dynamic Widths",
      "lectureOrder": 80,
      "videoOrder": 77,
      "sourceHash": "9094834e8cdc0e041dd60f350673a9dd42262802883346892a470a7ce7d97714",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.12,
          "end": 5.68,
          "en": "So how can we make everything a bit smaller?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.68,
          "end": 8.29,
          "en": "Let's maybe start with this game screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.29,
          "end": 10.163,
          "en": "This game screen is okay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.163,
          "end": 14.26,
          "en": "but some things are a little bit too big.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.26,
          "end": 17.445,
          "en": "For example, besides the position of that title, which,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.445,
          "end": 21.79,
          "en": "in my opinion, is a little bit too far at the top,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.79,
          "end": 26.08,
          "en": "we might wanna decrease the width of this a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.08,
          "end": 29.61,
          "en": "And if we have a look at our game screen, JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 32.22,
          "en": "there, we have various styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.22,
          "end": 34.36,
          "en": "But of course, for this title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.36,
          "end": 36.1,
          "en": "we don't have any specific styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.1,
          "end": 38.77,
          "en": "because data is a custom component stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.77,
          "end": 41.22,
          "en": "in the components UI folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.22,
          "end": 45.51,
          "en": "And if we go there, we see that in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.51,
          "end": 48.84,
          "en": "we have no real settings regarding the width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.84,
          "end": 51.48,
          "en": "that should be taken up by this title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.48,
          "end": 54.64,
          "en": "Instead, we basically take all the width we can get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.64,
          "end": 57.36,
          "en": "and the only spacing around it, this title, therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.36,
          "end": 60.4,
          "en": "is margin or padding applied to this title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.4,
          "end": 63.46,
          "en": "or to the container holding this title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.46,
          "end": 64.98,
          "en": "And that might be fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.98,
          "end": 69.83,
          "en": "but what we could do here, is we could give this a max width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.83,
          "end": 73.24,
          "en": "of let's say, 80%.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.24,
          "end": 74.71000000000001,
          "en": "And that then should be a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.71000000000001,
          "end": 76.533,
          "en": "so we should wrap it between quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.09,
          "end": 81.87,
          "en": "If we do this, then this title gets a bit smaller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.87,
          "end": 85.47,
          "en": "It's also not centered anymore because the parent container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.47,
          "end": 89.64,
          "en": "which uses Flexbox, because all views use Flexbox",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.64,
          "end": 93.87,
          "en": "in React Native doesn't center, its child items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.87,
          "end": 96.42,
          "en": "So we would have to go to the game screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 101.42,
          "en": "and then in there go to this view, this screen view",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.13,
          "end": 105.41,
          "en": "and make sure that all the children in there are centered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.41,
          "end": 109.593,
          "en": "by adding align items center here like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.45,
          "end": 114.36,
          "en": "And now that is all centered again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.36,
          "end": 116.94,
          "en": "Now it is up to you whether you like this or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.94,
          "end": 120.48,
          "en": "But what I wanna show you and emphasize is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.48,
          "end": 123.34,
          "en": "that you can use relative units like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.34,
          "end": 126.96,
          "en": "and we have used them before, to control widths and heights",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.96,
          "end": 130.38,
          "en": "and that you can not just set the width and height itself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.38,
          "end": 134.47,
          "en": "but that you can also set max width or min width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.47,
          "end": 139.443,
          "en": "besides the regular width to create more responsive sizes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.37,
          "end": 144.34,
          "en": "Because when you set the width, then it's always that width.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.34,
          "end": 147.32,
          "en": "It's now always 80%.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.32,
          "end": 151,
          "en": "With max width, it's up to 80%,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151,
          "end": 155.05,
          "en": "but it could be less if less space is needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.05,
          "end": 157.373,
          "en": "We could, for example, also set a width of,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 158.676,
          "end": 161.06,
          "en": "let's say, 300 pixels, which would be the default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 161.06,
          "end": 164.692,
          "en": "but we could then also at max width 80% to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.692,
          "end": 169.692,
          "en": "that 300 pixels is taken, unless that would be more than 80%",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 170.27,
          "end": 173.24,
          "en": "of the parent container, in which case the 80%",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.24,
          "end": 174.183,
          "en": "become active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.29,
          "end": 177.77,
          "en": "So with this on bigger screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.77,
          "end": 180.77,
          "en": "we can take a little bit more space, as you can tell by",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.77,
          "end": 183.1,
          "en": "the available space to the left and the right of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.1,
          "end": 183.933,
          "en": "the text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.933,
          "end": 187.4,
          "en": "There is less space available here on the smaller screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.4,
          "end": 190.34,
          "en": "On the bigger screen, this gap is wider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.34,
          "end": 193.92,
          "en": "But we only take the 300 pixels, which we seem to take here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.92,
          "end": 196.13,
          "en": "if there is enough space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.13,
          "end": 198.82999999999998,
          "en": "Here on the smaller screen, 300 pixels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.82999999999998,
          "end": 202.236,
          "en": "would be more than 80% of the available width,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.236,
          "end": 204.57,
          "en": "and therefor the 80% are taken instead since",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.57,
          "end": 205.76,
          "en": "that is our max width,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.76,
          "end": 208.23,
          "en": "and therefor the upper boundary of the width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.23,
          "end": 209.333,
          "en": "of this container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.29,
          "end": 212.61,
          "en": "And what's really important to note is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 212.61,
          "end": 215.81,
          "en": "that percentage settings like this always refer to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.81,
          "end": 219.14,
          "en": "the parent container that holds an element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 219.14,
          "end": 224.003,
          "en": "So, if I say at the title to a max width of 80%, those 80%",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 224.003,
          "end": 228.04,
          "en": "refer to the parent container that holds the title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.04,
          "end": 233.04,
          "en": "So, in this case to this view, because of this title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.43,
          "end": 236.123,
          "en": "this view is the parent container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.99,
          "end": 240.891,
          "en": "So, it's the width of this view of which 80% are taken by",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.891,
          "end": 244.9,
          "en": "the title because of this setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 244.9,
          "end": 248.87,
          "en": "So, percentage units and min and max width combined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 248.87,
          "end": 252.14,
          "en": "with the regular width can be very helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 252.14,
          "end": 254.04,
          "en": "And of course, it's not just about the width.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.04,
          "end": 257.07,
          "en": "You also have min at max height, in case you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 257.07,
          "end": 259.45,
          "en": "similar scenarios where you want to set a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.45,
          "end": 261.263,
          "en": "minimum or maximum height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.46,
          "end": 265.96,
          "en": "So, these extra style properties are properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 265.96,
          "end": 267.123,
          "en": "you should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
